{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And I will turn My hand.</b> Like הנה יד יהוה הויה (Exodus 9:3)." "<b>Borax.</b> As if it were borax-lye, but the correct interpretation is like כבור ידי (Psalms 18:25)." "The sense of <b>your dross</b> is because he said at the beginning, 'your silver has become dross.'" "Rabbi Moses the Kohen, may his memory be for a blessing, said that the seven types of metal are not found in Scripture in the plural form, yet he overlooked כל בדיליך."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "Resolved the epithet נ\"ע as 'may his memory be for a blessing' (נשמתו עדן)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:48.436902158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}